MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The N/Q1 real-PG proof at 61b93cff failed on five spec-authored expectations
while N and T agreed in every case. Correct the spec and its harness only:

- N02/N06: the inherited `failEvery` knob (`name='FAIL'`) was inert — no mapper
  reads the name. Replace it with `skipEvery`, staging every k-th row under the
  canonical but unregistered platform `auto:other.example`; the family dispatch
  records `skipped` / `unsupported_platform:auto:other.example` on both heads.
  Expectations follow from the fixture: 24 rows, k=6 -> 20/4 (both families);
  12 rows, k=4 -> 9/3 (clients), 12/0 (workouts). N==T tally equality kept;
  the skipped rows are asserted row by row (platform, status, null target,
  product reason).
- N03(a): reset the fixture before staging m1 (N01's rows were being counted).
  Stage a genuinely skipped sibling beside the reconstructed row in (a) and (c)
  so every mixed-writer pass carries one success and one non-success outcome;
  (d) asserts success dominates a later refusal from either writer with the
  sibling untouched; (e) adds the other order — a committed skip followed by a
  success from the other writer becomes reconstructed with its target.
- Q05: a scoped v2 token (or scope-bound legacy entities token) presented by a
  foreign coach or for a foreign intent is 400 `malformed cursor` with no page
  read and no reflection — decode runs before the settled-intent gate, as in the
  accepted R reader and the slice brief. Only the token-less request (and the
  scope-less legacy roster token) reaches the uniform 404 gate.

No product, schema, contract or migration change. The PG proof is not run here.
